meta {
  name: negative
}

docs {
  Adversarial and error-path requests: wrong client authentication method, malformed/garbage tokens, expired or misdirected client assertions, an unrecognized `authorization_details` type, and an unsupported grant type. Each documents an expected rejection — except `03-missing-scope` and `08-unknown-context-type`, which confirm a specific non-obvious success/silent-behavior case rather than a hard failure.

  See each request's own docs block for the exact behavior and its RFC/IG backing. Some requests here reuse tokens obtained in `auth/`.
}
